@startuml
skinparam linetype ortho
title SIC/XE Simulator - WebSocket /ws Protocol
autonumber
hide footbox

actor Frontend
participant "WebSocket /ws" as WS
participant "Server command handler" as Handler
participant "SessionStore" as SessionStore
participant Simulator
participant "SIC/XE Architecture" as CPU
participant Assembler
participant "Event manager" as Events

note over Frontend,WS
Request envelope:
{id, type: "command", payload: "..."}

The response echoes the request id.
end note

== Project synchronization ==
note over Frontend,SessionStore
Project files are synchronized through HTTP
before the project-load command is sent.
end note

== Project load ==
Frontend -> WS : load $session-id/project-id
WS -> Handler : validate envelope and dispatch
Handler -> SessionStore : get_project(sessionId, projectId)
SessionStore --> Handler : StoredProject
Handler -> Simulator : load_project(project)
Simulator -> CPU : select architecture and reset state
CPU -> Events : record reset / machine events
Simulator --> Handler : project and architecture info
Handler --> WS : {id, result: {project, arch}}
WS --> Frontend : Project-load response

== Source file load ==
Frontend -> WS : load %file-path
WS -> Handler : dispatch command
Handler -> Simulator : load_file(path)
Simulator -> CPU : load_file(source)
CPU -> CPU : clear current program state
CPU -> Assembler : assemble(source)
Assembler --> CPU : CodeMemory and AssemblyInfo
CPU -> CPU : install source map and set PC
CPU -> Events : memory, symbol and instruction-fetch events
note right of CPU
InstructionFetched may include:
- source_line (1-based)
- preview: true for debugger positioning
end note
Simulator --> Handler : EventBatch {from, to, events}
Handler --> WS : {id, result: EventBatch}
WS --> Frontend : Apply events

== Step ==
Frontend -> WS : step
WS -> Handler : dispatch command
Handler -> Simulator : step()
Simulator -> CPU : execute one instruction
CPU -> Events : fetch / execution / preview events
Simulator --> Handler : events array
Handler --> WS : {id, result: events[]}
WS --> Frontend : Apply events

== Reset and clear ==
alt reset
  Frontend -> WS : reset
  WS -> Handler : dispatch command
  Handler -> Simulator : reset()
  Simulator -> CPU : reset registers and PC
  CPU -> Events : reset and preview fetch events
  Simulator --> Handler : EventBatch {from, to, events}
  Handler --> WS : {id, result: EventBatch}
  WS --> Frontend : Apply events
else clear
  Frontend -> WS : clear
  WS -> Handler : dispatch command
  Handler -> Simulator : clear()
  Simulator -> CPU : clear program and machine state
  CPU -> Events : MemoryCleared / ProgramCleared / register events
  Simulator --> Handler : EventBatch {from, to, events}
  Handler --> WS : {id, result: EventBatch}
  WS --> Frontend : Apply events
end

== Error handling ==
alt malformed JSON
  Frontend -> WS : invalid JSON text frame
  WS --> Frontend : {id: null, error: problem}
else invalid envelope or unknown command
  Frontend -> WS : invalid request / unsupported payload
  WS -> Handler : validate or dispatch
  Handler --> WS : error response
  WS --> Frontend : {id, error: problem}
else state changed before command failure
  Handler -> Simulator : event_batch(eventStart)
  Simulator --> Handler : changed events (if any)
  Handler --> WS : problem plus optional events[]
  WS --> Frontend : apply events, then show problem
end

note over Frontend,Handler
Supported payloads are case-sensitive:
load $session-id/project-id
load %file-path
reset | clear | step

load project returns {project, arch}.
load file, reset, and clear return an event batch.
step returns the events array directly.
end note

note over CPU,Events
A normal InstructionFetched event indicates an executed fetch.
preview: true is an artificial debugger-positioning fetch,
not an instruction consumed by execution.
end note
@enduml
